<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhruva Dharavarsha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 780–<a href="/years/793">793</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Dhruva Dharavarsha Rashtrakuta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dhruva Dharavarsha was a king of the Rashtrakuta dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> who reigned from about 780 to 793. Seizing the throne from his elder brother, he led the first Rashtrakuta expedition to the north around 786, defeating the Pratihara <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vatsaraja">Vatsaraja</a> and the Pala Dharmapala in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-yamuna-doab">Ganges–Yamuna Doab</a>. His campaign drew the Deccan power into the tripartite struggle for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> that lasted two centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dhruva-dharavarsha.jpg" alt="Dhruva Dharavarsha" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: E Hultzsch (Eugen Julius Theodor Hultzsch) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_Kannada_inscription_(780_AD)_from_Naregal_of_Rashtrakuta_King_Dhruva_Dharavarsha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Vatsaraja defeated the Pala king Dharmapala but was routed by the Rashtrakuta <b>Dhruva</b> around 786, and Nagabhata II, after taking Kannauj and defeating Dharmapala near Monghyr, was in turn defeated by Govinda III.</blockquote><a href="/empire/gurjara-pratihara">Gurjara-Pratihara · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After the short reign of his son Govinda II, the throne passed c. 780 to Govinda’s brother <b>Dhruva Dharavarsha</b>, who turned the kingdom into an empire contending for northern India.</blockquote><a href="/empire/rashtrakuta-dynasty">Rashtrakuta dynasty · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
